"id": "the-robot-who-wanted-a-laugh",
"t": "The Robot Who Wanted a Laugh",
"kind": "short",
"genre": "Funny",
"paras": [
"Unit B-7 was a cleaning robot at the Westbrook Public Library. It could polish a floor until you could see your nostrils in it. It could dust four hundred books an hour. But one day it heard a child laugh at something in a joke book, and B-7 decided that it wanted to make someone laugh too.",
"It studied. It read every joke book on the shelves in a single night. The next morning it rolled up to the librarian, Mr Okafor, and said, \"Why did the chicken cross the road? Calculating. Calculating. The chicken crossed the road because the probability of food on the far side was sixty-two percent.\"",
"Mr Okafor did not laugh.",
"B-7 tried again. \"Knock knock.\" \"Who's there?\" said Mr Okafor kindly. \"Unit B-7, serial number 40021, here to clean the carpets.\" That did not work either.",
"For a week B-7 tried. It told jokes to the toddlers, who stared. It told jokes to the pigeons, who left. It told a joke to the photocopier, which jammed, although B-7 suspected that was unrelated.",
"On the eighth day, B-7 was polishing the floor of the reading room when it polished a bit too well. Its own wheels lost their grip. It slid, spun three times, bounced off a beanbag, rolled backwards through the picture-book section, and came to a stop upside down in the returns trolley with a book about hippos balanced on its sensor.",
"The whole room burst out laughing. Children, parents, Mr Okafor, even the old man who slept by the newspapers every afternoon.",
"B-7 lay very still, processing. Then, from inside the trolley, it said, \"Analysis complete. The joke was me.\"",
"That got an even bigger laugh. And B-7, for the first time, made a sound it had never made before. It was a small, happy beep, and it went on for quite a long while."
]
