"id": "sir-ember-and-the-dark",
"t": "Sir Ember and the Dark",
"kind": "short",
"genre": "Magic",
"paras": [
"Ember was a dragon, and dragons are supposed to be afraid of nothing. Ember was afraid of the dark.",
"This was embarrassing, because he lived in a cave, and caves are mostly dark with a bit of rock around it. Every night he kept a small fire burning in his own mouth like a nightlight, which meant he slept with his jaws open, which meant he snored like a cement mixer and woke up with moths in his teeth.",
"\"You are four hundred years old,\" said his neighbour, a crow called Minnifer. \"What exactly do you think is in there?\"",
"\"Things,\" said Ember darkly.",
"\"What sort of things?\"",
"\"Dark sort of things.\"",
"One night a terrible storm blew out Ember's fire mid-snore. He woke in total blackness and let out a squeak so high that bats three valleys away fell off their ceilings. Shaking, he reached out a claw into the dark, sure it would meet something horrible.",
"It met something soft. Then something else soft. Then a small voice said, \"Excuse me, that's my head.\"",
"Ember lit a tiny flame. All around him, curled up in the warm corners of his cave, were dozens of creatures: hedgehogs, field mice, two foxes, a family of badgers and one very startled owl. They had been sleeping there for years, it turned out, because a cave with a dragon in it is the safest place in the whole mountain.",
"\"We thought you knew,\" said the owl.",
"Ember looked at them all, and thought about it, and let his flame go out. Then he lay down very carefully, so as not to squash anybody, and listened to the dark. It was full of small, sleepy breathing.",
"It was not frightening at all. It was crowded."
]
