"t": "The Grand Snail Derby",
"kind": "short",
"genre": "Animals",
"paras": [
"Every summer the village of Lower Dawdle holds the Grand Snail Derby, and every summer it takes most of the afternoon.",
"This year there were six snails on the starting line. There was Thunderbolt, the champion, who belonged to the butcher. There was Lady Slime, who wore a tiny painted crown on her shell. There was Gary, who nobody had high hopes for. And there were three others, who wandered off sideways before the starting whistle and were never seen again.",
"The race was one metre long. The crowd roared. Thunderbolt took an early lead of nearly a centimetre. Lady Slime stopped to admire herself in a puddle. Gary went to sleep.",
"After forty minutes, the commentator, Mrs Biddle, had run out of things to say and had started reading out her shopping list. After an hour, the ice-cream van sold out. After an hour and a half, a wasp landed on Thunderbolt, and Thunderbolt went inside his shell to think about his life.",
"That left Lady Slime in front with twenty centimetres to go. The butcher wept. The crowd held its breath, which was a mistake, because she took another forty minutes.",
"Then, just as Lady Slime was nearly at the line, a single raindrop fell. Gary woke up. Gary loved rain more than anything in the world. Gary set off like a slimy arrow, overtook Lady Slime with a speed no one in Lower Dawdle had ever seen, and crossed the finish line at almost two centimetres per minute.",
"The crowd went wild. Gary was given a gold medal, which was much too big for him, and a lettuce, which was exactly the right size.",
"He ate the lettuce. Then he went back to sleep on the medal."
]
